// Phase 0 smoke test (Canton console bootstrap script).
//
// A standalone participant auto-initializes its identity on start. That initialization REQUIRES the
// rutli driver to:
//   (a) generate the namespace/identity key and node signing keys (generateSigningKeyPair), and
//   (b) SIGN the identity topology transactions (NamespaceDelegation, OwnerToKeyMapping) with the
//       namespace key via the driver's sign().
// If this script completes, the KMS Driver integration works end-to-end.
// Kept to minimal console API on purpose — println(x) over member-access pretty-printing.

println("=== rutli Phase 0 smoke test ===")

participant1.health.wait_for_initialized()

println("participant id (namespace = fingerprint of driver-held key):")
println(participant1.id)

println("public keys generated through the rutli driver:")
participant1.keys.public.list().foreach(k => println(k))

println("=== OK: identity initialized and topology signed via rutli ===")
